    "stem": "Yash measures a ribbon using the fractional unit $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ metre. Exactly $5$ of those units cover the ribbon end to end.\n\nWhich claim correctly writes the ribbon length?",
    "item_type": "mcq",
    "options": {
      "A": "The length is $5$ metres, taking only the count of units.",
      "B": "Say that writing $\\dfrac{5}{8}$ is what creates the unit size $\\dfrac{1}{8}$.",
      "C": "The length is $\\dfrac{5}{8}$ metre, because $5$ copies of $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ make $\\dfrac{5}{8}$.",
      "D": "The same reading $\\dfrac{5}{8}$ also fixes the length when a different unit such as $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ is chosen instead."
    },
